  "map.1.tutorial": "[TUTORIAL START] Try out movement, aiming and your primary and secondary weapon. Then push east: the route runs across marked checkpoints up to the extraction.",
  "map.2.tutorial": "Attacks can come from different directions. Watch the west and east fronts and switch sides before the pressure shifts. Demon Badgers heat up with every flame burst they spit, the glow spreading from head to tail. After the fifth they stop and melt down in a large red zone: kill them first or get out of the zone.",
  "map.3.tutorial": "Not every enemy attacks the base. Some hunt you directly—spot dangerous targets early and set your priorities. Rabid Rabbits pounce: when the ground ahead of you turns red, change direction before they land.",
  "map.4.tutorial": "The forward outpost supplies adrenaline and a BFG that needs time to charge. Use it against dense groups and protect the supply pedestals.",
  "map.5.tutorial": "Boss maps end only when the boss falls. Your first victory grants a boss point. This map unlocks Dachs Nukem and Dachs of Steel; Inspector stays locked.",
  "map.6.tutorial": "Three small spore turret outposts cover the approaches to the base. Fight within their range and move between fronts as the pressure shifts.",
  "map.7.tutorial": "Reach the end of the map to the east without dying.",
  "map.8.tutorial": "Keep the damaged rocket turret outposts alive until the marked HOLD assault ends to unlock the rocket turret permanently. You can still win the main mission if the Hold fails.",
  "map.9.tutorial": "No base. No retreat. Survive for 120 seconds. Enemies hunt you exclusively, and each player gets only two respawns.",
  "map.11.tutorial": "Enemy airstrikes are marked before impact. Keep moving and leave the target zones in time.",
  "map.12.tutorial": "Defending is no longer enough. The map only ends once the red enemy base is destroyed. Use the lulls between counterattacks to push forward. A wooden bridge spans the east river: fetch dynamite from the field cache and blow it with {key_interact}, and enemies can only reach the rear base through the south crossing. Anyone standing on the bridge falls with it.",
  "map.13.tutorial": "Thrower Badgers hurl brood bombs that hatch into new enemies. Optional brood nests add pressure—destroy them to make the remaining assault easier.",
  "map.14.tutorial": "Void fire spreads from the left and sets bases on fire too. Watch the violet warning rim, retreat through the corridors to the right and survive until the timer ends.",
  "map.16.tutorial": "Circle the lake clockwise to extraction in the east – each ford opens only once the ambush before it is beaten. Kaboomtulas rear up, rush in and leap at you: sidestep the leap at the last moment. Every enemy hunts you, not the base. Each player has three respawns.",
  "map.17.tutorial": "Beer is scattered on the way to the enemy base. Carry it back to the marked drop-off one bottle at a time. Each rescued bottle improves your reward—the beer is optional, the enemy base remains the main objective.",
  "map.18.tutorial": "Mortar badgers shell your base from range. The violet target ring marks the impact – get out of the ring and hunt the gunners before the next volley lands.",
  "map.19.tutorial": "Firestarter badgers fire lances and violet fire orbs. A lance that hits an orb detonates it into a firestorm. Dodge the warning line and keep the orbs away from your base.",
  "map.20.tutorial": "The kraken lurks in the Abyss Pond. Dodge tentacles, ink and spines, destroy the eggs before they hatch – and hold your ground when it comes ashore.",
  "map.tutorialStep.map01-adrenaline": "Hits with the left mouse button generate adrenaline. Collect it to use your stronger weapon with the right mouse button.",
  "map.tutorialStep.map01-utility": "Use your utility with {key_utility}. Hold {key_utility} to throw further. Destroy the rocks ahead of you to push further east.",
  "map.tutorialStep.map01-burrow": "Press {key_interact} to burrow. Burrowed you move faster, pass beneath rocks and dodge many attacks.",
  "map.tutorialStep.map01-rage": "Taking damage fills your rage. With enough rage the ultimate is ready and can be used with {key_ultimate}. Take damage or collect the power-up to build up enough rage.",
  "map.tutorialStep.map01-base-defense": "Many maps hold bases or outposts. Enemies attack them in waves – hold the position until both waves are defeated.",
  "map.tutorialStep.map01-extraction": "You have found your own base. Nobody knows why, but it follows you from map to map. Constructions built right next to the base remain standing.",
